 "derived_from": [],
 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Jameis signs up for his employer-based 401(k). The employer matches any 401(k) contribution up to 7.5% of the employee salary. Jameis’ annual salary is $72,800.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518417,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the most money that Jamie can deposit that will be fully matched by the company?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>An employer will match up to 7.5% of any employee’s salary.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{0}}{\\text{.075(72,500)  =  \\$5,460}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The amount Jamie can deposit that will be matched by the employer is $5,460.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$5,460"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 518418,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "How much total will be deposited into Jameis’ account if he deposits the full 7.5%?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The amount Jamie deposits plus the employer’s match: <span data-math=\"{\\text{5,460  +  5,460  =  \\$10,920}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The total is $10,920.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$10,920"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 518419,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "How much return does Jameis earn if he deposits exactly 7.5% in her 401(k)?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Jamie deposits $5,460. The account ends up with $10,920.</p>\n<p>The return on investment (ROI) is the percent difference between the initial investment (<i>P</i>) and the final value of the investment (<i>FV</i>), or <span data-math=\"{\\rm{ROI}} = \\frac{{FV - P}}{P}\"></span>, expressed as a percentage. The length of time of the investment is not considered in ROI.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\rm{ROI}} = \\frac{{10,920 - 5,460}}{{5,460}} = \\frac{{5,460}}{{5,460}} = 1 = 100\\% \"></span></p>\n<p>The ROI is 100%.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "100% return on the $5,460 deposit"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
